    stats: { enc: 2, dec: 2, ratio: 4, latency: 3, mem: 3, ra: 2, lossless: false },
    domains: ['image'],
    move: 'Split the image into a half-resolution approximation and three detail bands, then recurse on the approximation, so every scale nests in one coefficient array.',
    usedIn: ['JPEG 2000', 'DjVu', 'digital cinema (DCP)', 'FBI fingerprint archive'],
    why: 'No blocks, so no blocking artifacts; degrades into blur instead. Gives progressive decoding for free: the low-pass band is a thumbnail. Lost the web to JPEG anyway: patents, complexity, and "good enough".',
