    why: 'R, G and B are highly correlated: coding them separately codes the brightness three times. Luma plus two chroma channels separates "how bright" from "which colour", and the chroma channels compress far better. Integer-reversible versions exist, so this is fine for lossless coding too.',
    weakness: 'Small gain by itself; its main value is to enable chroma subsampling and separate quantization of the difference channels downstream.',
