    why: 'Sorting every rotation of the block and taking the last column puts letters that appear in the same contexts next to each other, turning text into runs. Move-to-front, run-length coding and Huffman then code those runs cheaply. Fully reversible with one extra index. It shows that a transform is not only for lossy signals.',
    weakness: 'Needs the whole block (900 KB in bzip2): no streaming, high latency, no random access. Beaten in ratio by context mixing and in speed by LZ77.',
